    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"environmental necessity\" argument feels a bit hollow when you're looking at the actual balance sheets of local companies. It feels more like a moral lecture than a real policy justification. If I'm being honest, it seems like the regulators are just prioritizing abstract global goals over the real, tangible survival of our local economy. Do you think their position is actually logically sound, or is it mostly just based on ideological pressure?",
